(RESERVE BANK OF INDIA) Tj
T*
(DEPARTMENT OF REGULATION, CENTRAL OFFICE, MUMBAI) Tj
T*
(RBI/2024-25/150 DOR.CRE.REC.11/21.01.005/2024-25) Tj
T*
(September 28, 2024) Tj
T*
(Framework for Acceptance of Green Deposits by Regulated Entities) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Scope and Currency Denomination: All scheduled commercial banks and deposit-taking NBFCs accepting green deposits must issue) Tj
T*
(such deposits denominated strictly in Indian Rupees \(INR\). Green deposits cannot be offered in foreign currency or under FCNR schemes.) Tj
T*
(2. Eligible Green Activities: Proceeds mobilized through green deposits must be earmarked exclusively for projects in eligible) Tj
T*
(green sectors: Renewable Energy \(solar, wind, biomass\), Clean Transportation \(electric vehicles and charging infrastructure\),) Tj
T*
(Energy Efficiency, Sustainable Water and Waste Management, Green Buildings certified by national/international rating systems,) Tj
T*
(and Terrestrial Biodiversity Conservation.) Tj
T*
(3. Excluded Activities: Green deposit proceeds shall not be allocated to projects involving extraction, production, or distribution) Tj
T*
(of fossil fuels, nuclear power generation, direct waste incineration, weapons, or tobacco cultivation.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /Length 893 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(4. Allocation Register and Third-Party Verification: REs must maintain a dedicated internal Green Deposit Allocation Register.) Tj
T*
(The allocation of green deposit proceeds must be subjected to an independent third-party external verification / assurance on an) Tj
T*
(annual basis by qualified environmental auditors.) Tj
T*
(5. Annual Impact Reporting: Regulated entities shall publish an Annual Impact Report on their website alongside their annual financial) Tj
T*
(statements. The report must disclose metrics such as estimated greenhouse gas \(GHG\) emissions avoided, renewable energy capacity) Tj
T*
(installed, and energy savings achieved per unit of capital allocated.) Tj
T*
(6. Board-Approved Policy: Banks offering green deposits must have a policy approved by the Board defining the framework for issuance) Tj
T*
(and tracking of funds.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
10 0 obj
<< /Length 902 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(7. Deposit Tenure and Pricing: Green deposits can be accepted as cumulative or non-cumulative term deposits with tenors ranging) Tj
T*
(from twelve months to one hundred twenty months. The interest rate offered on green deposits shall be determined in accordance with the) Tj
T*
(bank's overall Asset-Liability Management \(ALM\) framework.) Tj
T*
(8. Premature Withdrawal Rules: Premature withdrawal of green deposits shall be governed by existing regulatory guidelines applicable to) Tj
T*
(standard term deposits, without retroactively penalizing the green classification of funds already deployed in eligible projects.) Tj
T*
(9. Green Hydrogen and Energy Storage: Capital expenditure for green hydrogen production, electrolysers, and grid-scale battery energy) Tj
T*
(storage systems \(BESS\) is explicitly eligible for allocation of green deposit proceeds.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
11 0 obj
<< /Length 795 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(10. Independent Auditor Certification: The statutory auditors of the bank shall verify the compliance of the bank with the green) Tj
T*
(deposit framework and include a specific certification in the annual audit report.) Tj
T*
(11. Review by Board Committee: The progress of allocation of green deposit proceeds and the findings of third-party impact assessments) Tj
T*
(shall be placed before the Board's Risk Management Committee semi-annually.) Tj
T*
(12. Misallocation Remediation: In the event that a funded project ceases to qualify under eligible green criteria, the allocated proceeds) Tj
T*
(must be reallocated to another eligible project within ninety calendar days.) Tj
T*
(Yours faithfully,) Tj
T*
(\(Neeraj Nigam\)) Tj
T*
(Executive Director) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
